comment.body:
Closing in favour of #19595, which takes Paper the warm way: aged newsprint instead of fresh grey newsprint.

What carries over from this PR:

- primary actions printed as solid ink (reverse type);
- one spot red;
- syntax, diff and terminal colours by ink weight instead of a rainbow;
- every neutral as a screen of one ink.

What changes: the page moves from grey `#e9e6df` to a yellowed `#f3e7d3`, the ink from neutral carbon to a warm black, and the blue-black links and notes go away. Measured in OKLCH, this PR's page had less colour and less light than the old Paper, and its ink was almost neutral, which is what made it read cold. The light ochre warning here (`#c9a443`) also measured 1.9:1 as text; #19595 fixes that warning.

